  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "QCDIAG: fix memory allocation",
  "description": "Fix incorrect memory allocation.\n\nudp_bytes shall use wmem_alloc0().\n\nAs @johnthacker pointed out in !23708 , `udp_bytes` shall have proper memory allocation in `get_udp_hdr_tvb()`.\n\nCorrected: `udp_bytes = (uint8_t*)wmem_alloc0(pinfo->pool, udp_hdr_len);`\n\n> You cannot declare the real data on the stack. Allocate this with `pinfo->pool`, like with the other TVBs.\n\n> The lifetime of the TVB's data needs to be until the frame has finished processing, and the data can be used (e.g., for tshark to print or the GUI to show in the byte window) after this dissector returns.\n\nAdditional participant: @martin.r.mathieson",
  "state": "merged",
